  "overview": {
    "title": "Small dunes, real sand",
    "p1": "The Tinfou dunes will not rival Erg Chigaga in scale, but they offer real Saharan sand close to Zagora — climb, photograph, ride a short camel loop or simply watch the light change.",
    "p2": "On busy days it can feel like a playground; early or late visits are calmer. Combine with Tamegroute if you want culture and dunes in one outing.",
    "p3": "Bring water, closed shoes for hot sand, and a sense of proportion: this is an appetiser, not the whole desert."
  },
